{"page":1,"pageSize":100,"totalHits":1,"isTotalHitsExact":true,"sortBy":"id","sortOrder":"ascending","suggestion":[],"expandedEfoTerms":[],"expandedSynonyms":[],"query":"\"Interrogating the protein interactomes of RAS isoforms identifies PIP5K1A as a KRAS-specific vulnerability.\"","facets":null,"hits":[{"accession":"S-EPMC6128905","type":"study","title":"Interrogating the protein interactomes of RAS isoforms identifies PIP5K1A as a KRAS-specific vulnerability.","author":"Adhikari H Counter CM","links":4,"files":10,"release_date":"2018-01-01","views":16,"isPublic":true,"content":"S-EPMC6128905 PMC6128905 Interrogating the protein interactomes of RAS isoforms identifies PIP5K1A as a KRAS-specific vulnerability. In human cancers, oncogenic mutations commonly occur in the RAS genes KRAS, NRAS, or HRAS, but there are no clinical RAS inhibitors. Mutations are more prevalent"}],"nextCursor":null,"tooManyExpansionTerms":false}